sec.p:
We propose Prior-RDRGSE, a generative framework based on variational inference, whose core is to learn a generative model pθ(X,A,Y|ZA,ZY) that describes the dependency process of generating observed data from latent clean variables. Simultaneously, we introduce an inference network qϕ(ZA,ZY|X,A,Y) to approximate the posterior distribution of the latent variables. The entire model is optimized by maximizing the evidence lower bound and incorporates biological semantic priors and consistency constraints. The generative process is formally defined by the following conditional probabilities:
Structural Noise: A˜∼p(A˜|ZA,ES);
Feature Noise: X∼p(X|ZA,EF);
Label Noise: Y∼p(Y|ZA,X,EL).
